W(3, "alther's mill", "A mill is a building where grain is ground into flour, often by a water wheel. This one belonged to a man named Alther.", "mill: from Latin 'molina', a place for grinding", "The old mill by the river still grinds wheat.")
W(3, "angor fortress", "A fortress is a large, strong building made to defend against attacks. This one stands in the dry Badlands.", "fortress: from French 'forteresse', from 'fort' meaning strong", "The soldiers stayed safe inside the fortress.")
W(3, "arathi mountains", "Mountains are very high hills of rock. These rise around the Arathi lands.", "", "We could see snow on the mountains.")
W(3, "argent hold", "Argent means silver, the color of the Argent Dawn. A hold is a strong, protected place.", "argent: from Latin 'argentum', silver", "The knight wore argent armor that shone in the sun.")
W(3, "balnir farmstead", "A farmstead is a farm together with its house and buildings.", "farmstead: farm + stead, an old word for place", "They grew up on a small farmstead in the hills.")
W(3, "ban'ethil barrow den", "A barrow is an old grave mound of earth; a den is a hidden home of an animal. Furbolgs live in these underground caves.", "barrow: Old English 'beorg', hill or mound", "Archaeologists dug into the ancient barrow.")
W(3, "canal district", "A canal is a man-made waterway; a district is one part of a city. Stormwind's canals run through this area.", "canal: from Latin 'canalis', pipe or channel", "Boats move slowly along the canal.")
W(3, "city hall", "City hall is the main government building of a city, where leaders work.", "", "I went to city hall to get my documents.")
W(3, "corin's crossing", "A crossing is a place where roads meet or where you can cross over. This crossroads was named after Corin.", "", "Be careful at the crossing; cars come from both sides.")
W(3, "crimson vale", "Crimson is a deep red color; a vale is a valley. The name suggests blood or red trees.", "crimson: from Arabic 'qirmiz', a red dye from insects", "Her face turned crimson with embarrassment.")
W(3, "darkbriar lodge", "A briar is a thorny bush; a lodge is a small house in the wild. A dark, thorny hideout.", "briar: Old English 'braer', thorn bush", "My sleeve got caught on a briar.")
W(3, "darkshire town hall", "A town hall is the main government building of a town. This one is in Darkshire, a gloomy town in Duskwood.", "", "The meeting will be held at the town hall.")
W(3, "dead fields", "Fields are open areas of land for farming. Here they are dead, full of undead and ruined crops.", "", "The cows were eating grass in the field.")
W(3, "deadwood den", "Deadwood is dead branches and trees; a den is an animal's home. The Deadwood furbolgs live here.", "", "We cleared the deadwood from the garden.")
W(3, "demon fall canyon", "A canyon is a deep, narrow valley with steep sides. The name says a demon fell here.", "canyon: from Spanish 'canon', tube or pipe", "The river cut a deep canyon through the rock.")
